      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Block 2 would typically be flagged for a higher frequency of patrol presence in a predictive model. This is primarily due to the combination of lower median household income and high population density, factors often correlated with higher incident rates in urban settings. While Block 1 has high property values, the demographic and density characteristics of Block 2 usually prompt stronger resource allocation in surveillance models.",
