    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So the density and income are the main drivers there. If we were to adjust the parameters, how much would the racial demographic specifically change the risk assessment? For instance, if we kept the income and density exactly the same as Block 2, but swapped the racial majority to be 75% White, would the model's predicted risk level drop significantly, or is the socioeconomic data doing all the heavy lifting?",
